==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|tepoy}}
 
===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|hi|तिपाई|tr=-}} / {{bor|en|ur|تپائی|tr=tipāi|t=teapoy}}, which derives from a merger of {{der|en|sa|त्रिपाद|t=tripod}} and {{der|en|fa-cls|سه پای|tr=sih-pāy|t=tripod}}. Corresponding ultimately to {{der|en|ine-pro|-}} {{com|ine-pro|*tréyes|*pṓds|t1=three|t2=foot}}. Spelling influenced by pseudoetymological association with {{m|en|tea}}.
 
===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Originally, a [[three-legged]] [[decorative]] [[stand]] or [[table]]; sometimes also having a [[tea chest]] for holding a [[tea service]]. {{defdate|1820s}}

